  "post": {
    "caption": "Jade is two different minerals, nephrite and jadeite, which Alexis Damour told apart in 1863. Carvers in China worked jade more than 4,000 years ago, the Maya treated it as their most precious material, and in New Zealand nephrite is called pounamu. Jadeite comes mainly from Myanmar and Guatemala, and the finest translucent emerald green is called imperial jade.",
